@1000001 = ~Hello there! I thought I should tell you that Gorion has been looking to talk to <CHARNAME> and all of <PRO_HISHER> friends. You should go talk to Gorion as soon as possible.~
@1000002 = ~I hear your voice... you come into view.~
@1000003 = ~Canderous? Canderous Leighsfeld?~
@1000004 = ~Indeed, it has been a long time, old friend! We've not met for almost a decade. So this is where you have been serving all these years since you left Waterdeep.~
@1000005 = ~What of you, Canderous? Do you not intend to return and complete your training? I see your wound has long healed... our seniors would undoubtedly be pleased to see your return.~
@1000006 = ~I see. A worthy cause it is, and I am certain the monks of Candlekeep greatly value you for it. I respect your decision, my friend. Hopefully we may meet again in the future, outside of this castle.~
@1000007 = ~Aye, there's some books in the guest room for those who are bored and lookin' for something to read. It's got nothin' on the great library, of course, but it's somethin'. They be on the shelf, go ahead and take them, child. They're mostly gatherin' dust these days.~
@1000008 = ~We'd better move quickly, <CHARNAME>. There'll be more of these shapeshifting fiends ahead. Best watch for traps as well—who knows what's been done to this place.~
@1000009 = ~Don't worry, <CHARNAME>. We'll do everything we can to clear out these filth from Candlekeep's walls. You can rest assured of that.~
@1000010 = ~The path to the surface isn't far, <CHARNAME>. You'll be able to find your way out from here.~
@1000011 = ~I'm going to head back now. Someone'll need to report everything that's happened here. Sorry I can't help you more, but I know you'll be fine.~
@1000012 = ~Good luck, <CHARNAME>. Find the bastard who set this up and give him what he deserves... and come back alive.~
@1000013 = ~Well, well, young <CHARNAME>. It looks like you have finally arrived.~
@1000014 = ~I was hoping to speak with you one more time before you departed. I was taking my regular walk around the castle courtyard, you see, as I do every day, hearing the daily stories of all the good folk. And I have heard your name repeated often today, in particular.~
@1000015 = ~So be it. Go and speak with Gorion then, child. Take care of yourself in the world outside, and... I wish you good luck, for the trials ahead.~
@1000016 = ~Well, that would certainly depend on who I have asked. But you have certainly left a good impression on the day of farewell, it seems, with the many simple favors you have made. Delivering swords, bolts and books for the Watchers, clearing rats from peevish Reevor's storehouse, even curing Dreppin's poor cow...~
@1000017 = ~Your journey is an urgent one, young <CHARNAME>, and you have seen blood from those who would do you harm even here, where it should be safest. And yet, I am glad to see you have not forgotten to give a helping hand to those who ask.~
@1000018 = ~I cannot be sorry enough that we could not have done more for you, child. You will face many dark days ahead, I will not lie, and even with Gorion at your side, your trials will only be greater... but to the end, I hope you will never lose your heart, and always be willing to continue helping others, no matter how petty the concern.~
@1000019 = ~Nor do I hope that you ever forget that you are the pride of Candlekeep. Treasure your memories and experiences of this place—of your home and those who call you their friend—and look forward with courage. One day, everyone will welcome your safe return, with your heart and mind abundant with newfound wisdom.~
@1000020 = ~Now go, child. Gorion is waiting for you. I do not doubt that we will meet again.~
@1000021 = ~From Mordaine? To me? Okay, let me have a look...~
@1000022 = ~Oh. Oh... um, well... right, er... thanks for delivering it. I've got to get things ready, quickly...~
@1000023 = ~Calm yourself, Arkanis. There was reason to keep this secret from the Watchers, as well. Until we had full knowledge of the threat, some things had to be kept secret.~
@1000024 = ~Aye... don't trust a word from anyone else we find here... I'll put my axe through their skulls first. Fear not, child... we'll see you through this.~
@1000025 = ~Bah! Lies, <CHARNAME>, heed them not. The Watchers never heard anyone speak of such a thing!~
@1000026 = ~By Moradin's hammer! Young Hull, too? This is truly a waking nightmare...~
@1000027 = ~This is as far as we can go, my <PRO_GIRLBOY>. The Watchers must know of what has transpired here... but the end of the path will not be too far ahead.~
@1000028 = ~It pains us that we cannot protect you any further, but you have grown much since you first left. Even though your journey will undoubtedly only become more difficult... I can see you won't need the two of us any longer.~
@1000029 = ~Aye... this is goodbye once more, but I know we will meet again, someday.~
@1000030 = ~Go now, <PRO_GIRLBOY>... go, and live well.~
@1000031 = ~From what I hear, you're also an aspiring arcanist. You almost remind me of myself as a fledging apprentice, such a nostalgic time... I feel as your senior in the practice of the Art, I should do more for you, especially as I hear you will be going on quite the journey.~
@1000032 = ~Though I do not wish to overreach in your development as a mage, I can still give you a head start... here, I have an assortment of spell scrolls that may be useful to you. Pick one, any one. Will it be the scroll of Burning Hands, Friends, Spook, Protection from Evil, or Shield?~
@1000033 = ~Here you are, young one. This is but the beginning—the greater secrets of the Weave are out there. Me, I am far too old to be seeking them. But you have immeasurable potential. Good luck.~
@1000034 = ~Oho, and I see a familiar face taggin' along with you too. Imoen, girl, does my memory fail me, or did I not entrust you with the cleanin' of the rooms upstairs, eh?~
@1000035 = ~Now, haven't I always told you to be honest to your old man? You're spendin' time with <CHARNAME> before <PRO_HESHE> goes, I don't mind it. Just make sure you don't forget before the day's through, aye? You know this old back ain't as good at bendin' over to reach the corners as it used to be.~
@1000036 = ~That's a good girl.~
@1000037 = ~Don't say anything. Just run. I'll be with you soon. You should not see what is to come.~
@1000038 = ~<CHARNAME>, my child...~
@1000039 = ~Perhaps. But I do wonder, however... is this your idea of revenge, boy?~
@1000040 = ~You are a consequence of my past failures. Despite your posturing, you invoke no fear in me, only shame.~
@1000041 = ~You are right that I have failed too many times... but for the last, you are wrong. I have saved that child from becoming a slave to power, as you have. True, <PRO_HISHER> path will be difficult... but <PRO_HESHE> will have hope. Unlike you.~
@1000042 = ~Do what you will, but this will be no victory for you. That child is strong... the day will come when <PRO_HESHE> reaches heights you never shall.~
@1000043 = ~Enough taunts. The debt between us is long overdue... it's high time we settled it at last.~
@1000044 = ~Sa—~
@1000045 = ~Even in your final moments, you deceive <PRO_HIMHER>. You know full well how this will end.~
@1000046 = ~The past is irrelevant. When I look upon what has become of you and your ward, I consider myself blessed that I was not cursed with such weakness.~
@1000047 = ~But you are well-versed in failure, are you not, old man? You could not save that woman, or the others... and once you are dead, you will not be able to save that whelp.~
@1000048 = ~Indeed? Perhaps I should keep one last breath of life in you instead, so that you will be there to witness the day I properly crush your hope under my heel...~
@1000049 = ~Ah... so you do have a speck of your former fire within you after all. This will be more entertaining than I expected.~
@1000050 = ~Yes, I know. Our time is precious, and our plan is only at its inception. We shall make this quick.~
@1000051 = ~Is that so? Challenge accepted, old man. I shall anticipate the struggle that is to come... a pity you will not be alive to witness it.~
@1000052 = ~Woof!~
@1000053 = ~I see you are here with the... young <CHARNAME>. I take it that means you intend to leave soon, as you've so stubbornly insisted?~
@1000054 = ~Well, I would wish you safe journey, but I doubt that will be the case, given what I know of your intentions. Perhaps you have reconsidered since our last discussion?~
@1000055 = ~Foolish... I have said it before, Gorion. There is a much simpler solution to this inanity. You and I know this to be true.~
@1000056 = ~I would have thought age and comfort would have ridded you of your urge for meddling in affairs that are beyond you. You have chosen peace for all these years, and you will throw it all away for your sentimentality?~
@1000057 = ~Bah! ~
@1000058 = ~Fine. On your own head be it, foolish Harper.~
@1000059 = ~If you are set in your absurd ways, then I shall not expect either of your returns with optimism. But I will repeat my generous advice—you would do best to leave <PRO_HIMHER> in some forgotten ravine and be done with it.~
@1000060 = ~Now then, you two have a long journey to take, and I have proper business to attend to. Out of my way.~
@1000061 = ~Gorion.~
